{"version_id": 62, "article_id": 7, "level_code": "en_a2", "lang": "en", "level": 2, "level_label": "A2 初级", "title": "Former German spy chief arrested for spying", "title_zh": "德国前情报局长因间谍罪被捕", "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c58jzyer1kr0o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/Helmut_Schmidt%2C_former_German_Chancellor.jpg", "credit": "No machine-readable author provided. Axel Sperl assumed (based on copyright clai · cc0 1.0 · via wikimedia"}, "published_date": "2026-10-06", "word_count": 185, "reading_minutes": 0.9, "lead": "A former head of Germany's intelligence service has been arrested. Police say he gave secret information to other countries.", "lead_zh": "德国情报机构的前负责人被捕。警方称他向其他国家提供了秘密信息。", "preview": "August Hanning is a former spy chief in Germany. He led the BND from 1998 to 2005. After that, he worked as a private consultant. Now police", "preview_zh": "奥古斯特·汉宁是德国前情报局长。1998年到2005年，他领导联邦情报局（BND）。之后，他做私人顾问。现在警方逮捕了他。他们说，他犯了间谍罪和叛国罪。他还被指控为外国势力获取机密信息。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 52, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@a79b424/content/audio/7/en_a2.mp3", "duration": 83.638, "size_bytes": 505584, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 211, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@a79b424/content/data/versions/62.json", "paragraphs": ["August Hanning is a former spy chief in Germany. He led the BND from 1998 to 2005. After that, he worked as a private consultant. Now police have arrested him. They say he committed espionage and treason. He is also accused of getting classified information for a foreign power.", "Police also arrested a former BND employee, called Manfred D. He worked for the BND until this year. Police say he gave Hanning about 2,000 classified documents. He did this in exchange for money. Manfred D was Hanning's bureau chief. Later, he was chief of staff for Hanning's successors.", "Prosecutors say Hanning used secret information to write an analysis for a foreign intelligence officer. He also had close contact with another foreign intelligence service for many years. He gave them political information. Investigators did not say which countries were involved.", "Local media reported that Hanning was arrested at his home in Nordwalde. Manfred D was arrested in Bavaria. Hanning will go to court on Wednesday. Manfred D will appear on Tuesday. The BND has had similar problems before. In 2023, another officer was charged with treason."], "paragraphs_zh": ["奥古斯特·汉宁是德国前情报局长。1998年到2005年，他领导联邦情报局（BND）。之后，他做私人顾问。现在警方逮捕了他。他们说，他犯了间谍罪和叛国罪。他还被指控为外国势力获取机密信息。", "警方还逮捕了一名前BND员工，叫曼弗雷德·D。他在BND工作到今年。警方说，他给了汉宁大约2000份机密文件。他这样做是为了换钱。曼弗雷德·D曾是汉宁的办公室主任。后来，他给汉宁的继任者当幕僚长。", "检察官说，汉宁用秘密信息为一名外国情报官员写了一份分析报告。多年来，他还与另一个外国情报机构保持密切联系。他给了他们政治信息。调查人员没有说涉及哪些国家。", "当地媒体报道，汉宁在诺德瓦尔德附近的家中被捕。曼弗雷德·D在巴伐利亚被捕。汉宁将于周三出庭。曼弗雷德·D将于周二出庭。BND以前也遇到过类似问题。2023年，另一名官员被控叛国罪。"], "body": "August Hanning is a former spy chief in Germany. He led the BND from 1998 to 2005. After that, he worked as a private consultant. Now police have arrested him. They say he committed espionage and treason. He is also accused of getting classified information for a foreign power.\n\nPolice also arrested a former BND employee, called Manfred D. He worked for the BND until this year. Police say he gave Hanning about 2,000 classified documents. He did this in exchange for money. Manfred D was Hanning's bureau chief. Later, he was chief of staff for Hanning's successors.\n\nProsecutors say Hanning used secret information to write an analysis for a foreign intelligence officer. He also had close contact with another foreign intelligence service for many years. He gave them political information. Investigators did not say which countries were involved.\n\nLocal media reported that Hanning was arrested at his home in Nordwalde. Manfred D was arrested in Bavaria. Hanning will go to court on Wednesday. Manfred D will appear on Tuesday. The BND has had similar problems before. In 2023, another officer was charged with treason.", "body_zh": "奥古斯特·汉宁是德国前情报局长。1998年到2005年，他领导联邦情报局（BND）。之后，他做私人顾问。现在警方逮捕了他。他们说，他犯了间谍罪和叛国罪。他还被指控为外国势力获取机密信息。\n\n警方还逮捕了一名前BND员工，叫曼弗雷德·D。他在BND工作到今年。警方说，他给了汉宁大约2000份机密文件。他这样做是为了换钱。曼弗雷德·D曾是汉宁的办公室主任。后来，他给汉宁的继任者当幕僚长。\n\n检察官说，汉宁用秘密信息为一名外国情报官员写了一份分析报告。多年来，他还与另一个外国情报机构保持密切联系。他给了他们政治信息。调查人员没有说涉及哪些国家。\n\n当地媒体报道，汉宁在诺德瓦尔德附近的家中被捕。曼弗雷德·D在巴伐利亚被捕。汉宁将于周三出庭。曼弗雷德·D将于周二出庭。BND以前也遇到过类似问题。2023年，另一名官员被控叛国罪。", "text": "August Hanning is a former spy chief in Germany. He led the BND from 1998 to 2005. After that, he worked as a private consultant. Now police have arrested him. They say he committed espionage and treason. He is also accused of getting classified information for a foreign power. Police also arrested a former BND employee, called Manfred D. He worked for the BND until this year. Police say he gave Hanning about 2,000 classified documents. He did this in exchange for money. Manfred D was Hanning's bureau chief. Later, he was chief of staff for Hanning's successors. Prosecutors say Hanning used secret information to write an analysis for a foreign intelligence officer. He also had close contact with another foreign intelligence service for many years. He gave them political information. Investigators did not say which countries were involved. Local media reported that Hanning was arrested at his home in Nordwalde. Manfred D was arrested in Bavaria. Hanning will go to court on Wednesday. Manfred D will appear on Tuesday. The BND has had similar problems before. In 2023, another officer was charged with treason.", "vocab": [{"word": "spy", "pos": "noun", "zh": "间谍", "note": "指从事秘密情报工作的人"}, {"word": "chief", "pos": "noun", "zh": "负责人；局长", "note": "常用于职位名称，如 spy chief"}, {"word": "arrest", "pos": "verb", "zh": "逮捕", "note": "常用被动语态 be arrested"}, {"word": "treason", "pos": "noun", "zh": "叛国罪", "note": "法律用语，指背叛国家"}, {"word": "classified", "pos": "adj", "zh": "机密的", "note": "指政府或军队的秘密信息"}, {"word": "document", "pos": "noun", "zh": "文件", "note": "可数名词，复数 documents"}, {"word": "foreign", "pos": "adj", "zh": "外国的", "note": "常与 country, service 等搭配"}, {"word": "court", "pos": "noun", "zh": "法庭", "note": "go to court 意为出庭"}], "title_original": "Former German spy chief arrested for espionage and treason", "summary_original": "August Hanning is accused of obtaining classified information for a foreign power.", "body_original": "Former German spy chief arrested for espionage and treason\nBy\nOlivia Ireland\nPublished\n6 hours ago\nFormer German spy chief August Hanning has been arrested on suspicion of espionage, treason and obtaining classified information for a foreign power, the German Federal Prosecutor's Office says.\nHanning headed the Federal Intelligence Service (BND) from 1998 to 2005 and has since been working as a private consultant.\nProsecutors allege that he used classified intelligence to \"draft an analysis\" for one foreign intelligence service and maintained contact with another foreign spying service. Investigators have not disclosed which foreign powers were involved.\nPolice also arrested former BND employee Manfred D, accusing him of passing Hanning about 2,000 classified documents for money.\nManfred D, who was Hanning's bureau chief and remained in the BND until this year, is charged with aiding and abetting attempted treason and treasonous espionage.\nLocal media reported Hanning was arrested at his home in Nordwalde near Münster while Manfred D was arrested in Bavaria. Hanning is due in court on Wednesday and Manfred D will appear on Tuesday.\nProsecutors say Manfred D, who also served as the chief of staff for Hanning's successors between 2012 and 2026, used his role to gain access to highly confidential information which he then passed on to Hanning \"in exchange for remuneration\".\n\"The current findings suggest that, over the years, Manfred D provided Hanning with approximately 2,000 documents, many of which contained classified information to be used exclusively by the Federal Intelligence Service for internal purposes,\" the statement says.\n\"On one occasion, Hanning used classified intelligence ... to draft an analysis for an officer of a foreign intelligence service,\" prosecutors said, noting it was not clear if \"the material reached the intended recipient\".\nHanning is also accused of being \"in close contact with a representative of another foreign intelligence service, to whom he passed on political information, partially based on material provided by Manfred D, for several years\".\nLocal media say Hanning's alleged possession of intelligence documents came to light during a separate case relating to German steakhouse heiress Christina Block.\nHamburg public prosecutor's office accused Block of orchestrating the kidnapping of her two youngest children in 2023 due to a custody dispute. Investigators allege Hanning was involved in an earlier attempted kidnapping of the children, which he denies.\nState criminal police officers reportedly discovered an electronic data storage device containing sensitive information including recent BND documents.\nIt is not the first time the BND has faced similar controversy. A high-ranking German intelligence officer was\ncharged with treason in 2023\nfor allegedly passing state secrets to Russia.\nProsecutors alleged Carsten L shared intelligence about the war in Ukraine and the Wagner mercenary group and received roughly €400,000 ($450,000; £340,000). His trial is ongoing.\nRelated topics\nGermany\nCorruption\nSpying\nMore on this story\nAlmost 60,000 far-right extremists in Germany, intelligence agency says\nPublished\n30 June\nGermany investigates Russia links to weapons cache discovered in woods, reports say\nPublished\n21 August", "fetched_at": "2026-10-06T16:57:31.470498+00:00", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "August", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.525, "sm": 100, "em": 525, "cs